# soul-audio-core commit the DAP CI builds against (the `soul-audio-core` /
# soul-audio-engine / soul-audio-index path deps resolve to THIS revision in CI).
#
# Why a pin, not a floating branch: building CI against soul-audio-core@main makes
# every DAP PR's result depend on when it runs — an unrelated soul-audio-core merge
# can turn a green PR red on re-run (non-reproducible). Pinning a rev makes CI
# deterministic and makes picking up soul-audio-core changes a DELIBERATE, reviewed
# bump (tools/soul-audio-core-pin.sh). Local dev is unaffected: dap/ keeps the
# sibling PATH dep, so your working copy of ../../soul-audio-core is what builds
# locally — this pin only governs CI.
#
# One line, the full 40-char SHA. Update with: tools/soul-audio-core-pin.sh --set <sha>
9cf69fdb0ee6f53c7b04bb872d97e2c4c86ef015
